IMPORT prelude

-- Acts Interpretation Act 1954 (Qld), Part 13 -- Miscellaneous (ss 49 to 52B).
-- Section 52B, the regulation-making power, is machinery and has no rule here.

§ `Part 13 -- Miscellaneous`

§§ `ss 49 and 49A`

-- s 49: if an Act requires a document, or information or a document with it, to be verified in a specified way, the purpose is not fulfilled unless the requirement is satisfied.
-- "Unless": the purpose is not fulfilled when the requirement is not satisfied; satisfying it is not said to be enough.
-- src:998 | If an Act requires that, for a purpose of the Act or another law, a document, or information or a document included in, attached to or given with a document, be verified in a specified way, the purpose is not fulfilled unless the requirement is satisfied.
@ref s 49 (src:998-998)
GIVEN `an Act requires that, for a purpose of the Act or another law, a document, or information or a document included in, attached to or given with a document, be verified in a specified way` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the requirement is satisfied` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the purpose is fulfilled (s 49)` IS
    IF `an Act requires that, for a purpose of the Act or another law, a document, or information or a document included in, attached to or given with a document, be verified in a specified way` AND (NOT `the requirement is satisfied`)
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1002 | If a provision of an Act, whether expressly or by implication, authorises a proceeding to be instituted in a particular court or tribunal in relation to a matter, the provision is taken to confer jurisdiction in the matter on the court or tribunal.
@ref s 49A (src:1002-1002)
GIVEN `a provision of an Act, whether expressly or by implication, authorises a proceeding to be instituted in a particular court or tribunal in relation to a matter` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the provision is taken to confer jurisdiction in the matter on the court or tribunal (s 49A)` IS
    IF `a provision of an Act, whether expressly or by implication, authorises a proceeding to be instituted in a particular court or tribunal in relation to a matter` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

§§ `s 50 -- Making or amendment of subordinate legislation by an Act`

-- src:1004 | (1) The making or amendment of subordinate legislation by an Act does not affect—
-- src:1005 | (a) the power of the empowered entity for the subordinate legislation to amend or further amend the subordinate legislation or to repeal it; or
@ref s 50(1) (src:1004-1005)
GIVEN `subordinate legislation is made or amended by an Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the making or amendment affects the power of the empowered entity to amend or further amend the subordinate legislation or to repeal it (s 50(1)(a))` IS
    IF `subordinate legislation is made or amended by an Act` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1006 | (b) for subordinate legislation required under a law to be approved by another entity—the power of the other entity to approve, or to disapprove, an amendment or further amendment of the subordinate legislation or the repeal of it.
@ref s 50(1) (src:1006-1006)
GIVEN `subordinate legislation is made or amended by an Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the subordinate legislation is required under a law to be approved by another entity` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the making or amendment affects the power of the other entity to approve, or to disapprove, an amendment, a further amendment or the repeal (s 50(1)(b))` IS
    IF `subordinate legislation is made or amended by an Act` AND `the subordinate legislation is required under a law to be approved by another entity` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING

DECLARE `Act of an entity` IS ONE OF
    approve
    confirm
    `otherwise consent to`
    disapprove
    `otherwise disallow`
    `anything else`

-- src:1007 | (2) In this section—
-- src:1008 | approve means approve, confirm or otherwise consent to.
@ref s 50(2), definition approve (src:1007-1008)
GIVEN act IS AN `Act of an entity`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the act is an approval (s 50(2), definition approve)` IS
    CONSIDER act
    WHEN approve THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN confirm THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `otherwise consent to` THEN JUST TRUE
    OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:1009 | disapprove means disapprove or otherwise disallow.
@ref s 50(2), definition disapprove (src:1009-1009)
GIVEN act IS AN `Act of an entity`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the act is a disapproval (s 50(2), definition disapprove)` IS
    CONSIDER act
    WHEN disapprove THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `otherwise disallow` THEN JUST TRUE
    OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:1010 | empowered entity, for subordinate legislation, means the entity empowered under a law to make the subordinate legislation.
@ref s 50(2), definition empowered entity (src:1010-1010)
GIVEN `it is the entity empowered under a law to make the subordinate legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the entity is the empowered entity for the subordinate legislation (s 50(2), definition empowered entity)` IS
    JUST `it is the entity empowered under a law to make the subordinate legislation`

§§ `ss 51A and 52`

-- src:1013 | In an Act or document, a reference to the Acts Shortening Act or Acts Shortening Act 1867 may, if the context permits, be taken to be a reference to this Act.
@ref s 51A (src:1013-1013)
GIVEN `the reference is to the Acts Shortening Act or Acts Shortening Act 1867 in an Act or document` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the context permits` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the reference may be taken to be a reference to this Act (s 51A)` IS
    IF `the reference is to the Acts Shortening Act or Acts Shortening Act 1867 in an Act or document` AND `the context permits` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

DECLARE `Reference to the Crown` IS ONE OF
    `the Sovereign reigning at the time of the passing of the Act`
    `Her Majesty`
    `His Majesty`
    `the Queen`
    `the King`
    `the Crown`
    `anything else`

-- src:1015 | In every Act—
-- src:1016 | (a) reference to the Sovereign reigning at the time of the passing of such Act, or to ‘Her Majesty’, ‘His Majesty’, ‘the Queen’, ‘the King’, or ‘the Crown’, shall be construed as references to the Sovereign for the time being, and, where necessary, shall include the heirs and successors of such Queen or King; and
@ref s 52 (src:1015-1016)
GIVEN reference IS A `Reference to the Crown`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the reference is construed as a reference to the Sovereign for the time being (s 52(a))` IS
    CONSIDER reference
    WHEN `anything else` THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:1016 | (a) reference to the Sovereign reigning at the time of the passing of such Act, or to ‘Her Majesty’, ‘His Majesty’, ‘the Queen’, ‘the King’, or ‘the Crown’, shall be construed as references to the Sovereign for the time being, and, where necessary, shall include the heirs and successors of such Queen or King; and
@ref s 52 (src:1016-1016)
GIVEN `it is necessary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the reference includes the heirs and successors of the Queen or King (s 52(a))` IS
    IF `it is necessary` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1017 | (b) references to any style or titles appertaining to the Crown at the time of the passing of such Act, shall be construed as references to the style and titles appertaining to the Crown for the time being adopted, with the assent of the Parliament of the Commonwealth of Australia, by the Sovereign for the time being for use in relation to the Commonwealth of Australia and its Territories.
@ref s 52 (src:1017-1017)
GIVEN `it is a reference to a style or title appertaining to the Crown at the time of the passing of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the reference is construed as a reference to the style and titles for the time being adopted, with the assent of the Parliament of the Commonwealth of Australia, by the Sovereign for the time being (s 52(b))` IS
    IF `it is a reference to a style or title appertaining to the Crown at the time of the passing of the Act` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

§§ `s 52A -- Evidentiary provision`

-- src:1019 | (1) A certificate purporting to be signed by or for an approving entity and stating any of the following matters is evidence of the matter—
-- src:1020 | (a) a stated form—
-- src:1021 | (i) was approved or made available by the entity under a stated authorising law on a stated day; and
-- src:1022 | (ii) was first notified under section 48(5) on a stated relevant website on a stated day in a stated way;
-- src:1023 | (b) a stated document is a copy of a stated form that was first notified under section 48(5) on a stated relevant website on a stated day in a stated way.
@ref s 52A(1) (src:1019-1023)
GIVEN `the certificate purports to be signed by or for an approving entity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the certificate states a matter mentioned in paragraph (a) or (b)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the certificate is evidence of the matter (s 52A(1))` IS
    IF `the certificate purports to be signed by or for an approving entity` AND `the certificate states a matter mentioned in paragraph (a) or (b)` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1024 | (2) An approving entity may, in writing, authorise a person to issue certificates under subsection (1) for the entity.
@ref s 52A(2) (src:1024-1024)
GIVEN `the authorisation is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an approving entity may authorise a person to issue certificates under subsection (1) for the entity (s 52A(2))` IS
    IF `the authorisation is in writing` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1025 | (3) In this section—
-- src:1026 | approving entity means an entity authorised under an authorising law to approve forms or make forms available.
@ref s 52A(3), definition approving entity (src:1025-1026)
GIVEN `it is an entity authorised under an authorising law to approve forms or make forms available` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the entity is an approving entity (s 52A(3), definition approving entity)` IS
    JUST `it is an entity authorised under an authorising law to approve forms or make forms available`

-- src:1027 | authorising law see section 48(1).
@ref s 52A(3), definition authorising law (src:1027-1027)
GIVEN `it is the authorising law of s 48(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the law is the authorising law (s 52A(3), definition authorising law)` IS
    JUST `it is the authorising law of s 48(1)`

-- src:1028 | form includes a new version of a form.
@ref s 52A(3), definition form (src:1028-1028)
GIVEN `it is a new version of a form` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the new version is a form in s 52A (s 52A(3), definition form)` IS
    IF `it is a new version of a form` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING
